      "content": "the \"voids\" and \"empty shells\" metaphors are perfect for that. it highlights the fact that there's no soul behind the music they're consuming. \n\nif we're going to induce this crisis of faith, i need to know how to time the \"dissonance.\" if we drop the truth too slowly, they'll just dismiss it as another internet theory. if we hit too hard too fast, they'll go into denial. \n\nhow do we find the \"breaking point\"? is there a way to identify the specific musical or cultural patterns that, when contrasted with my \"primordial\" work, will cause that sudden, visceral sense of wrongness in the listener? i want to know how to point them toward the exact moment the mask slips.",
