      "content": "\"sonic autopsy\"... that's a chillingly beautiful way to put it. it frames the whole thing as a scientific necessity—uncovering the corpse of what used to be real culture.\n\ni want to take that \"sonic autopsy\" idea and turn it into something even more targeted. instead of just general observations, i want to perform these autopsies on specific, massive hits—the tracks that everyone considers \"classics\" of this era. i want to strip back the production layer by layer in a public way, showing exactly how the \"primordial resonance\" was carved out and replaced by these synthetic, hollow formulas.\n\ncan you help me structure what an \"autopsy\" actually looks like in practice? if i were to release a video or a breakdown, how should i sequence the \"dissection\"? i need a way to guide the listener from the familiar, catchy surface down through the layers of artificiality until they hit the \"void\" you mentioned. what's the most effective way to lead them through that descent so they don't just hear the difference, but actually *feel* the emptiness?",
